    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Saturated Steam Properties Reference\n\n### Key Parameters\n- **Absolute Pressure (bar)**: The absolute pressure of the saturated steam\n- **Boiling Point (°C)**: The saturation temperature at the given pressure\n- **Specific Volume (m³/kg)**: Volume occupied by 1 kg of steam at saturation\n- **Density (kg/m³)**: Mass per unit volume of steam\n- **Specific Enthalpy of Liquid Water (kJ/kg)**: Sensible heat required to heat water from 0°C to saturation temperature\n- **Specific Enthalpy of Steam (kJ/kg)**: Total heat content of saturated steam\n- **Latent Heat of Vaporization (kJ/kg)**: Heat energy required to convert liquid water to steam at constant temperature and pressure\n- **Specific Heat (kJ/kg·K)**: Heat capacity of the substance\n\n### Important Notes\n- **Vacuum Steam**: Saturated steam at temperatures below 100°C operates at pressures lower than atmospheric pressure\n- **Pressure Relationship**: As pressure increases, the saturation temperature increases, and the latent heat of vaporization decreases\n- **Specific Volume**: Decreases with increased pressure - higher pressure allows more energy transfer in steam distribution systems\n- **Standard Atmospheric Pressure**: 1 bar abs = 0 bar gauge = 100 kPa abs (IUPAC system)\n\n### Example Applications\n\n**At 1 bar (Atmospheric Pressure)**\n- Water boils at 100°C\n- Sensible heat to reach saturation: 417.51 kJ/kg\n- Latent heat of vaporization: 2257.92 kJ/kg\n- Total enthalpy of steam: 2675.43 kJ/kg\n\n**At 8 bar Absolute Pressure (7 bar gauge)**\n- Water boils at 170.42°C\n- Sensible heat to reach saturation: 720.94 kJ/kg\n- Latent heat of vaporization: 2046.53 kJ/kg (less than at atmospheric pressure)\n- Total enthalpy of steam: 2767.46 kJ/kg\n"
    }
